1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:09,800
H-JEPA: Hierarchical World Models for Visual Planning.

2
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:13,400
Encode observations and actions.

3
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:16,800
Build a hierarchy across timescales.

4
00:00:16,900 --> 00:00:21,800
Train jointly: each higher level predicts
farther ahead in its own learned latent space.

5
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:25,667
Higher levels abstract away fast details.
AntMaze representations retain position.

6
00:00:25,733 --> 00:00:29,867
In FourRoom, the controlled agent remains
while the moving distractor fades.

7
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:33,500
Encode the current observation and the goal.

8
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:37,000
Plan toward the goal at a coarse level.

9
00:00:37,100 --> 00:00:42,300
High-level predictions become subgoals.
Refine them into primitive actions.

10
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:45,800
Act, observe and replan.

11
00:00:46,300 --> 00:00:52,800
FourRoom, Visual AntMaze, Push-T and Cube:
LeWM and H-JEPA example executions, alongside the goal.

12
00:00:53,300 --> 00:00:57,000
Success versus planning compute:
Pareto plots across four simulated environments.

13
00:00:57,100 --> 00:01:00,800
Three levels lead on navigation and Cube;
two levels work best on Push-T.

14
00:01:01,300 --> 00:01:05,000
DROID: planning from real-world robot video.
Inverse-dynamics supervision plus a learned hierarchy.

15
00:01:05,100 --> 00:01:08,800
More faithful plans across diverse scenes.
Offline evaluation of end-effector paths against expert trajectories.

16
00:01:09,300 --> 00:01:15,900
H-JEPA: Learn abstractions. Plan ahead.
Paper and code at h-jepa.com.
